# ============================================================
#  Expansion — more generic relationship events (actor: any).
# ============================================================

@event soc_lost_notes
title: The Borrowed Notes
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where not tagged(npc, faculty) and rel(npc) >= 3
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: scroll
tags: social study
scene: A student holding a single soggy page of notes, the rest of the stack floating away down a stream behind them.
text: {npc} borrowed your Lore notes last week. {They} {are} now standing in front of you holding a single soggy page. "There was a stream," {they} say{s}. "And a duck. Mostly a duck."
> left: Laugh it off
  gold -tiny
  rel npc +medium
  study -tiny
  say: You rewrite your notes from memory. {npc} brings you a cake every day for a week, by way of apology. The cakes are better than the notes were.
> right: Make {them} rewrite them
  gold -tiny
  rel npc -tiny
  study +tiny
  say: {npc} copies out forty pages from a friend's notes, grumbling. The new notes are neater than yours ever were.

@event soc_birthday
title: A Birthday
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 9 and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 12
art: gem
tags: social festival
scene: A small cake with a single candle in a dark common room, a group of students crouched behind a sofa, a surprised face in the doorway.
text: You find out — by accident — that it's {npc}'s birthday. {They} haven't told anyone. {They} {are} spending it in the library, alone, on purpose.
> left: Organise a surprise
  gold -small
  rel npc +large
  mood +small
  say: Seven people jump out from behind a sofa. {npc} screams, then laughs, then has to sit down. "How did you know?" You'll never tell.
> right: Join {them} in the library
  rel npc +medium
  lore +tiny
  say: You sit down opposite {them} with your own book. Neither of you says happy birthday. At midnight {they} slide{s} a biscuit across the table, and you both grin.

@event soc_bad_news
title: Bad News From Home
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 12 and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 12
art: letter
tags: social
scene: A student sitting on a stone staircase with a crumpled letter, head bowed, a friend sitting down beside them.
text: {npc} is sitting on the stairs with a letter in {their} lap, not moving. {Their} grandmother is ill. The barge home takes two days. "I don't know whether to go," {they} say{s}.
> left: "Go. We'll cover your classes."
  rel npc +large
  study -tiny
  say: {npc} catches the next barge. You take notes for two in every lesson. When {npc} comes back, {their} grandmother is better, and {they} hug{s} you on the landing.
> right: Just sit with {them}
  rel npc +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: You sit there until the stairs move under you. You don't fix anything. That's not what {they} needed.

@event soc_stargazing
title: Counting Stars
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and rel(npc) >= 12 and bond(npc) != "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: star
tags: social romance
scene: Two students lying on their backs on a flat roof, close but not quite touching, a sky full of stars above.
text: {npc} has dragged a blanket up to the roof. "There's a meteor shower," {they} say{s}. "Supposedly." There's room on the blanket for two, just about.
> left: Count meteors
  gold -tiny
  rel npc +medium
  mood +small
  say: You count thirty-one. {npc} counts thirty-four and accuses you of not looking properly. You weren't, entirely.
> right: Talk about everything else
  gold -tiny
  spark npc +small
  rel npc +small
  say: You don't see a single meteor. You talk about home and fear and what you'd do if you could do anything. When you look up, the sky's gone grey with dawn.

@event soc_jealous_friend
title: Jealousy
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where (bond(npc) == "friend" or bond(npc) == "close")
per: npc
trigger: social
when: known() >= 4
repeat: 10
art: mask
tags: social
scene: A student standing alone at the edge of a laughing group, arms folded, watching someone else take what used to be their seat.
text: {npc} has been odd all week. Finally it comes out. "You've got all these new friends now. I just — I don't know where I fit anymore."
> left: Reassure {them}
  health -tiny
  rel npc +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You tell {them} exactly where {they} fit: right here, first. {npc} rolls {their} eyes, but {they}'re smiling. The oddness is gone by dinner.
> right: Tell {them} friendship isn't a contest
  health -tiny
  rel npc -tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: You're right, technically. {npc} knows it. It still lands badly. It takes a few weeks for things to feel easy again.

@event soc_teach_spell
title: A Trick Worth Learning
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 7
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: wand
tags: social magic
scene: Two students in an empty classroom, one demonstrating a wand movement, the other copying it with a tiny spark of light.
text: {npc} has a spell {they} invented — a little thing, half-useful, half-ridiculous — and wants to teach it to someone. "It makes your tea exactly the right temperature," {they} say{s}. "Forever."
> left: Learn it properly
  health -tiny
  arcana +small
  rel npc +small
  say: It takes an hour. Your tea is now perfect, always. You'll use this spell more than anything you learn in class.
> right: Teach {them} one of yours in return
  health -tiny
  rel npc +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You trade spells like secrets. By midnight you've both got a new trick and an inside joke that will last three years.

@event soc_secret_admirer
title: A Secret Admirer
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and spark(npc) >= 15 and bond(npc) != "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 12
art: letter
tags: romance
scene: A folded note tucked into a library book with a pressed flower, unsigned, the handwriting careful and slightly shaky.
text: Folded notes keep appearing in your library books. Unsigned. They're funny, and a little nervous, and they know things about you that only someone paying attention would know. The handwriting looks familiar.
> left: Leave a note back
  spark npc +small
  say: You write back. The notes get longer. One day the last line just says: "It's {npc}. You knew, didn't you?" You did.
> right: Stake out the library
  challenge deceive trivial:
    win:
      spark npc +medium
      rel npc +small
      say: You catch {npc} red-handed, mid-tuck. {They} turn{s} the colour of a pyromancy exam. You both laugh until the librarian throws you out.
    lose:
      spark npc +tiny
      say: You wait three nights and catch nobody. On the fourth morning the note says: "Nice try."

@event soc_injured_friend
title: Carried
class: routine
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 6 and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 10
art: cross
tags: social danger
scene: A student carrying another piggyback across a muddy lawn, the injured one's ankle wrapped in a scarf.
text: {npc} has twisted an ankle on the far side of the grounds, a long way from the infirmary, and it's getting dark. {They} {are} trying very hard to pretend it doesn't hurt.
> left: Carry {them} on your back
  vigor +small
  rel npc +medium
  health -tiny
  say: It's a long way. {npc} narrates the whole journey like a horse race. By the time you reach the infirmary you're both laughing too hard to breathe.
> right: Run for help
  alignment +tiny
  rel npc +small
  say: You run for Sister Amaranth, who arrives with a floating stretcher and a lot of opinions. {npc} is fine. {They} send{s} you a thank-you sweet.

@event soc_rival_decency
title: An Unexpected Kindness
class: routine
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where (bond(npc) == "rival" or bond(npc) == "nemesis" or rel(npc) <= -9) and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 10
art: hand
tags: rival social
scene: A student picking up a rival's scattered books from a wet floor, the rival frozen mid-step, not sure what to say.
text: You drop your books in the rain, and the first person to stoop and help pick them up is {npc}. {They} hand{s} them back without a word, looking as surprised as you are.
> left: Thank {them} properly
  gold -tiny
  rel npc +large
  say: "Don't make it a thing," {npc} mutters. But the next day {they} nod{s} to you in the corridor. Something has thawed.
> right: Suspect a trick
  health -tiny
  rel npc -tiny
  guile +tiny
  say: You check the books for hexes. There aren't any. {npc} saw you checking. You'll both remember that.

@event soc_partner_anniversary
title: An Anniversary
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner" and spark(npc) >= 40
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 12
art: ring
tags: romance
scene: Two people on a bench by the lake at sunset, one holding out a small wrapped box, the other's hands over their mouth.
text: It's been a while now — long enough that {npc} has started calling things "ours". Today {they} hand{s} you a small wrapped box and won't meet your eyes.
> left: Open it now
  gold -tiny
  spark npc +small
  mood +medium
  say: Inside: a pebble from the lakeshore where you first really talked, polished to a shine. "It's stupid," {npc} says. It isn't. You carry it everywhere.
> right: Give {them} yours first
  gold -small
  spark npc +medium
  mood +medium
  say: You'd had the same idea. You both open your boxes at once. They're nearly the same gift. You laugh until the sun goes down.
